-- title:
--   Vanishing q-expansion forces vanishing at a supersingular point
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q\ge 5$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a nonunit of $A$. Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ an element whose image lies in $A$, and write $A_0$ for the preimage of $A$ in $k_0$; assume $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring whose maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, that $A_0$ is henselian, that its residue field is algebraically closed, and that every element of $A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$. Fix a further prime $\ell'\neq q$ with $\ell'\ge 3$ and $\ell'\nmid M'$, an element $\xi\in k_0$ that is a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity, and assume some ring embedding $k_0\to\mathbb C$ carries $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell'))$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $k_0((q))/k_0$ obtained as `laurentBaseChange`, i.e. generated over $k_0$ by the coefficientwise images of the function field `xHFunctionField` of level $(q\ell')^2M'$ with $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell')^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell')^\times$, equipped with an $A_0$-algebra structure compatible with $A_0\subseteq k_0\subseteq K$, and let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent series the image of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) under `coeffEmb`. Let $y'$ be a maximal ideal of the $A_0$-subalgebra $C'=$ `chartAlgFin` $A_0\,K\,j$ of $K$ which contains the image of $\pi_0$, and assume $y'$ is supersingular: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi\colon C'\to\Omega$ with kernel $y'$, the value $\varphi(j)$ lies in `ssJSet` $q\,\Omega$, that is, every elliptic curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\varphi(j)$ has no nonzero point killed by $q$. Then every $h\in C'$ all of whose Laurent coefficients (indexed by $n\in\mathbb Z$) lie in the maximal ideal $\pi_0A_0$ of $A_0$ belongs to $y'$.
--
--   This is the $q$-expansion principle in the form needed for the semistable fibre analysis at level $q\ell'$: on the special fibre of the two-chart integral model the branch through the cusp $\infty$ passes through every supersingular point, so an element whose $q$-expansion reduces to zero modulo $\pi_0$ vanishes at each supersingular closed point. It is used by the auxiliary-level results [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.mem_asIdeal_of_coe_mem_nonunits_gaussValuationSubring_of_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.mem_asIdeal_of_coe_mem_nonunits_gaussValuationSubring_of_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.mem_of_forall_coeff_mem_maximalIdeal_of_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.mem_of_forall_coeff_mem_maximalIdeal_of_mem_ssJSet_twoChartIntegralModel), and rests on the Gauss valuation subring attached to the $q$-expansion together with the supersingular-point statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.mem_of_coe_mem_nonunits_of_isMaximal_of_mem_ssJSet_chartAlgFin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.mem_of_coe_mem_nonunits_of_isMaximal_of_mem_ssJSet_chartAlgFin).
